If you're generating AI influencer content, dataset images, or anything through a ComfyUI pipeline, your source generations are never coming out full resolution. Upscale them wrong once and you're introducing artifacts. This episode builds a complete SeedVR2 upscale setup from a blank canvas, node by node, both an image pipeline and a video pipeline sitting on the same workflow. No downloaded JSON, no copy-paste template, you'll actually understand what every setting does.

What we cover:
Loading images single file or full batch folder, and switching between the two with one node
Picking the right SeedVR2 model size for your actual VRAM, from 8GB up to 24GB and beyond
Building the image upscale pipeline start to finish with a fixed seed for reproducible output
Adding a fully separate video upscale pipeline on the same canvas, its own loaders, its own settings
Getting frame rate handled automatically instead of hardcoding a number that breaks on different source clips
Common mistakes people make with resolution targeting and max_resolution safety ceilings


